              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Gujarati for the groom's procession, then the Gujarati for to marry off."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: વિદાય",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "વિદાય — vidāy — \"a farewell; the bride's send-off\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "દીકરીની વિદાય વખતે માતા રડી પડી. dīkrīnī vidāy vakhte mātā raḍī paḍī. At her daughter's send-off the mother burst into tears."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "વિદાય (vidāy) is recorded by Monier-Williams as Sanskrit vidāya, \"permission to go away, dismissal with good wishes\", with a note that in this sense it is perhaps not a Sanskrit word at all and a comparison with Arabic wadāʿ, \"farewell\"; its history is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
